(Chapter 1: Solutions) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(1.1 Introduction) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(A solution is a homogeneous mixture of two or more components. The component) Tj
T*
(present in the largest quantity is called the solvent. The component present in) Tj
T*
(smaller quantity is called the solute. A binary solution has two components: one) Tj
T*
(solute and one solvent.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Solutions can be classified by the physical state of the solvent into solid,) Tj
T*
(liquid, and gaseous solutions. The most common type in chemistry is the liquid) Tj
T*
(solution where the solvent is a liquid.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(1.2 Types of Solutions) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Definition: A saturated solution is a solution in which no more solute can) Tj
T*
(dissolve at a given temperature.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Definition: An unsaturated solution is a solution in which more solute can be) Tj
T*
(dissolved at the same temperature.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Definition: A supersaturated solution is an unstable solution containing more) Tj
T*
(solute than the saturation amount at the given temperature.) Tj
